  data: {
    LLM: "Player to dealer's left leads. Must follow suit if able. If an opponent is winning, you must beat their card if possible when following suit. If void, must trump if possible (unless partner is winning).",
    Player: "Player to dealer's left leads. Must follow suit if able. If an opponent is winning, you must beat their card if possible when following suit. If void, must trump if possible (unless partner is winning).",
    objective: "Be the first team to collect 101 points or more. One game to 101 is called a 'boam' (tree).",
    gameplay: "Player to dealer's left leads. Must follow suit if able. If an opponent is winning, you must beat their card if possible when following suit. If void, must trump if possible (unless partner is winning).",
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if able. If opponent is winning, must beat their card when following suit or overtrump when void; if partner is winning, no obligation to beat or trump.',
      'Undertrumpping is illegal (cannot play a lower trump than the one winning the trick unless only small trumps left).',
      "Dealer chooses trump (or no trump for double); no bidding. Dealer's partner must not look at cards before trump is chosen.",
      'First team to 101 points wins one boam. Card points: 10=5, A=4, K=3, Q=2, J=1; 9/8/7=0. Team with more points in tricks scores (total minus 30); doubles apply for no trump, Ik ga mee, tie, or all tricks.',
